      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87488",
      ":question/problem": "The graph of $y = 4f(2x) - 3$, can be obtained from the graph of $y = f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(T1)$ - Translate up by $3$ units\n- $(T2)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n- $(T3)$ - Translate down by $3$ units\n- $(T4)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $0.5$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?"
