      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87490",
      ":question/problem": "The graph of $y = 8f(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{3}{2})$, can be obtained from the graph of $y = f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(T1)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n- $(T2)$ - Translate up by $\\frac{3}{2}$ units\n- $(T3)$ - Translate left by $3$ units\n- $(T4)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $8$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?"
